{
  "title": "NDSC Website - Information Architecture / Sitemap",
  "version": 2,
  "source": "Reconstructed from an XMind mind map. v1 from a screenshot (NDSC_Website.jpg); v2 updated against a later text export (REGISTER.pdf) reflecting edits made to the live map.",
  "notes": [
    "This mind map is the source-of-truth sitemap for the Notre Dame Science Club (NDSC) web platform.",
    "Node shapes in the original diagram carry meaning: rounded rectangles = pages/sections, parallelogram = data input/upload, circle (o) = a generic connector/process step with no label, dashed boxes = data-structure notes (not pages), strikethrough text = collapsed/duplicate reference to a node defined elsewhere in the tree (not re-expanded to save space). Shape info could not be re-verified in v2 since the update source was plain text, not an image.",
    "Four small diagrams in the tree are NOT connected by lines to the main tree - they are floating reference/legend diagrams that define shared concepts reused all over the tree (the form system, shared data models, and two workflows). They are included under 'reference_diagrams' and 'workflows' and are cross-referenced from the main tree via 'ref' fields.",
    "Some labels in the source diagram appear to be typos or placeholders left by the original author; these are preserved verbatim with an 'original_label' plus a 'note' where it seemed useful, rather than silently corrected.",
    "Changes made in v2 vs v1: added a stage note under DASHBOARD; removed the 'history' branch from Profile; moved 'Recent Post' from Submission/History to Social; fleshed out ADMIN > Activities > Enrollments (Basic Data, From Config, FORM SYSTEM) in place of the old 'Subtopic 2' placeholder; substantially expanded ADMIN > Social (Voting/Chats/Survays/Mailing/WP Messaging + new 'Sponsorship messaging', each now with history/responses, plus a filtering note); added a new 'Social_Response' data entity to Veriable Structures."
